ions with a collapsible description panel[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every AXE lumberjack and chop description authored by the sase-9t [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]epic becomes a rich multi-line document with a one-line summary and[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]an explanatory body, the shared Rust config authority owns and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]enforces that grammar, and the ACE AXE tab renders the full [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]description in a beautiful accent-gutter panel that a new `d` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]keymap collapses to its summary line and expands again.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]axe_multiline_descriptions.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core owns the description grammar[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_description_grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_description_grammar: teach sase_core's AXE config authority the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]summary/body description grammar — add a `split_axe_description` binding[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that normalizes and splits one description, add flag-gated shape [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics for a blank summary, an over-long summary, a missing blank [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]separator line, and an over-long description, and release the crate.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plumb summary and body through sase and turn on shape [/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]enforcement[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sase_description_parts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_description_grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase_description_parts: bump the sase-core-rs window, wrap the new split[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in the chop facade, carry `description_summary` / `description_body` on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the AXE config dataclasses and TUI snapshots, add `maxLength` to both [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]description schemas so editors switch to a multi-line text area, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flip `require_description_shape` on in the sase compose and mutation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collapsible AXE description panel and the `d` keymap[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]axe_tab_panel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase_description_parts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]axe_tab_panel: rebuild the AXE description banner as a two-state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accent-gutter panel that word-wraps the body, renders bullet blocks, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]caps its height honestly; add the `d` toggle keymap with its config [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default, tab gating, footer, help, and palette registration; and cover [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]it with unit and PNG snapshot tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Summary-first AXE CLI listings[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli_surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase_description_parts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli_surfaces: keep `sase axe chop list` and `sase axe lumberjack list` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on one summary line per entry so tables stay scannable, and add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`-v/--verbose` full-description rendering to both.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rewrite every builtin lumberjack and chop description[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]builtin_descripti